":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T12:47:26-07:00","id":267614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=267451#post267451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;Thread necromancy&amp;quot; is when you try to bring back a thread by posting something stupid and useless like &amp;quot;I agree LOL&amp;quot;. When you use instead solid and new arguments to revitalize the thread, it can be considered &amp;quot;True resurrection&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no true resurrection, there is only Zuul.<br /> <br /> But seriously, don't necromance kids-just start a new thread and link back to the old one as an inspiration. And think hard before doing even that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-04-2014, 12:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T14:14:46-07:00","id":268527,"title":"","content":"I adore Leviathan's mood and feel, but I'm not exactly in love with its mechanics or the specifics of the setting. That's part of the reason I'm so excited for Beast; I think it will do what I wish Leviathan did.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T09:22:13-07:00","id":272283,"title":"","content":"I Like Genius for the Most Part.. Always got abit Confused about the Inventions.. But i Love it. I like the Idea of a Couple of Others.. But Not Really got into them.. Well Except for the Idea of Sailor Moon by Way of Cthulu that is Princess...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T18:06:56-07:00","id":275913,"title":"","content":"It hasn't been mentioned but I've been waiting for the completion of Psychic: the Gifted for years. Damn it looked nice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=266035#post266035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know why, but I have a small aversion to Fan-Splats. For some reason, they never *click* with me.</div> </div> </div> </div>And comments like this getting the most #&amp;@ing upvotes is why I hate these #&amp;@ing boards with all of my heart.<br /> Never EVER expect an objective view except maybe in one of the side comments around here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2330-vree","name":"Vree","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T18:17:52-07:00","id":275917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=275913#post275913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And comments like this getting the most #&amp;@ing upvotes is why I hate these #&amp;@ing boards with all of my heart.<br /> Never EVER expect an objective view except maybe in one of the side comments around here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking as a frequent user of the substance, I must point out that this is excessive vitriol for what is a very mild statement of personal preference in a thread about personal preferences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T18:25:56-07:00","id":275923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=275913#post275913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It hasn't been mentioned but I've been waiting for the completion of Psychic: the Gifted for years. Damn it looked nice.<br /> <br /> <br /> And comments like this getting the most #&amp;@ing upvotes is why I hate these #&amp;@ing boards with all of my heart.<br /> Never EVER expect an objective view except maybe in one of the side comments around here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why is what Griautis said a problem? Nevermind the fact that your hostility is really unwarranted and fairly rude to everyone else that frequents the boards, why is it unfair to say that there's something about a lot of fan splats that doesn't click for you?<br /> <br /> Moreover, is it a problem that other people share this view? Does it in any way denigrate the work those people put into their fan splats? It feels like you're assuming the worst of a fairly mild post.<br /> <br /> I'm also stuck on this notion of an &quot;objective view.&quot; What does that mean in the discussion of fanwork? Is it really an appropriate expression in a thread about personal favorites?<br /> <br /> I think it'd be nice if you could explain a bit of what's going on in this post, as I don't understand why you &quot;hate these #&amp;@ing boards&quot; as much as you seem to. Is it because of a seeming aversion to fansplats? Do you perceive elitism in that, or is it something else? Help us out and give some context for all this vitriol.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 10-08-2014, 09:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T19:00:35-07:00","id":275971,"title":"","content":"First off.<br /> <br /> It's fucking. Either go all the way with your curse or don't bother. THis is not actually important and you are free to ignore it, it's just a peeve of mine.<br /> <br /> Second.<br /> <br /> Griatus expressed a common sentiment with a nicely respectful approach. I know I have the same problem-even Princess I never really clicked with(I got close though), and none of the others got half as close. Back to the comment, it wasn't hateful or degrading, it's not like he went &quot;OMIGAWD FANGAMES SUCK&quot;. He just admitted to a problem that reflects on his relationship to the game, not the game itself, which lots of people sympathize with.<br /> <br /> Third.<br /> <br /> It doesn't come up often, but I have to ask myself if that sort of vitriol comes up in regards to standard produced WoD games. I'm fairly sure you were there, so where were you when I had my big &quot;Man, Requiem never clicked with me&quot; spliel. If I had my friend come in and say &quot;So, I don't like Demon the Descent, Mummy The Curse, Vampire the Requiem, or Promethean the Created, they just don't click for me&quot;, would you go &quot;OMIGAWD YOU PEOPLE RUIN THE BOARDS&quot;? Is it strictly because there's a popular consensus?<br /> <br /> I'm just looking for consistency here.<br /> <br /> Let's clarify-I don't think anyone has said anything bad about fangames. We've said it's not for us, which is fine, because it's kinda like how anal beads aren't for everyone(weird comparisons are weird). Getting all bent out of shape over that is bad form.<br /> <br /> But seriously, Genius's entire design philosophy is screwed up, and design by committee is a terrible way to make games.*<br /> <br /> Now you have someone being a dick. I'll be here all week.<br /> <br /> *Although it must be said that I have no idea if they actually by and large turned out okay or not, but design by committee has a lot of problems to it that contribute to the stigma of fan-splats, justified or not. And while I don't know if Genius is good or not, I will say that having learned the design philosophy of it's founders, I have the double problem of not being interested in that piece and objecting to it as a matter of principle. Don't let this dissuade you though-I'll be here all week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T19:02:19-07:00","id":275973,"title":"","content":"Boy you guys would be easy to troll. :I Just let the comment go. You didn't even have to respond to it.<br /> I have aired my negative opinion about the boards before so it isn't exactly news. I can explain it again some other time.<br /> If I offended your sensibilities, my bad.<br /> <br /> Just keep chatting about on topic stuff and stop worrying so much. I don't have the patience for this bs and I don't want you to derail the thread.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2330-vree","name":"Vree","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T19:21:16-07:00","id":275981,"title":"","content":"I'm down with that.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">but still, you <i>did</i> start it.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T20:04:16-07:00","id":276015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=275981#post275981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm down with that.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">but still, you <i>did</i> start it.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>So? You don't have to respond to and correct everything that people say. That's a bad habit.<br /> I mean, 3 lenghty comments in like half an hour, seriously to like one sentence. -_- Let people think what they do and move on. You guys should go back and delete them.<br /> Feel free to add this to my complaints about this board as well.<br /> I wanted to add some more comments on games but seriously, this.<br /> <br /> Will try to respond to one comment.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=275971#post275971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">design by committee is a terrible way to make games.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's Leviathan etc. Genius was a solo job.<br /> <br /> All the canon games are made by committee though. You can't skip playtesting &amp; such either. So what are you even saying.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=275971#post275971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And while I don't know if Genius is good or not</div> </div> </div> </div>So you haven't even read it. I have zero interest in advertising it to you or convincing you but seriously. Why diss stuff you never checked. facepalm/shrug","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2330-vree","name":"Vree","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T20:16:13-07:00","id":276020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=276015#post276015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All the canon games are made by committee though. You can't skip playtesting &amp; such either. So what are you even saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>They have a lead designer, who makes the design decisions, which is the opposite of committee design. They might take the comments of writers under advisement but it's ultimately their decision what happens or doesn't happen.<br /> <br /> In a game designed by committee, said committee makes the decision collectively. I imagine what's being suggested is having a lead designer who makes sure everything is coherent and falls within the &quot;vision&quot; of the game is a good idea, rather than allowing several people with different, sometimes competing ideas of what a game is decide all of its parts on a case by case basis, as this risks creating a product which lacks cohesion.<br /> <br /> For what it's worth, while I don't think I've seen anyone that's officially some kind of lead designer (as official as one can be for a fansplat, anyway) I have seen people generally deferring to project leads when it comes to fansplats.<br /> <br /> As a question related to my earlier comment, has anyone made any fan templates that are more equivocal to the Purified? I'm intrigued by the concepts of a bunch of fan splats (The one that comes to mind is Pathogen, I think it's called?) but a little put off by the desire to force them into the mold of fuller splats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T20:21:45-07:00","id":276022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=276015#post276015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, 3 lenghty comments in like half an hour, seriously to like one sentence. -_- Let people think what they do and move on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find it difficult to seriously parse &quot;literally one sentence less than two lines long&quot; as &quot;lengthy,&quot; but your lumping dissent together is duly noted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All the canon games are made by committee though. You can't skip playtesting &amp; such either. So what are you even saying. </div> </div> </div>You're confusing having multiple writers with having no real developer oversight when the entire point of a developer is seeing to it that the writers' work agrees with itself in aggregate and with the intended vision in general.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So you haven't even read it. I have zero interest in advertising it to you or convincing you but seriously. Why diss stuff you never checked. facepalm/shrug </div> </div> </div>Vree, learning that the point of genesis of a thing was &quot;I think this okay thing sucks&quot; is a plenty reasonable rationale for aversion to that thing. I agree with his assessment <i>and Genius was my introduction to nWoD.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T20:33:08-07:00","id":276029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=276020#post276020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a question related to my earlier comment, has anyone made any fan templates that are more equivocal to the Purified? I'm intrigued by the concepts of a bunch of fan splats (The one that comes to mind is Pathogen, I think it's called?) but a little put off by the desire to force them into the mold of fuller splats.</div> </div> </div> </div>On that note, what happened to the Highlander type (Immortal: Gathering I think?) splat? I heard a rumor that it was removed due to WW's copyright claim (conflicting with Immortals or something?)<br /> I think it may have had a similar set up to what you're asking too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2330-vree","name":"Vree","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T20:45:21-07:00","id":276035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=276015#post276015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you haven't even read it. I have zero interest in advertising it to you or convincing you but seriously. Why diss stuff you never checked. facepalm/shrug</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a weird grey area. I don't know if it's good or not. People seem to like it, it seems to have gained traction and has a decently sized fanbase for what it is, which is impresive in our already niche culture. I have good reason to believe it might actually be good.<br /> <br /> I'm not dissing the game. I can't, because I don't know.<br /> <br /> I am, however, dissing the principles that informed its' creation. I object to that sort of mentality. Games are art, they invite connection, and they should do so because a person has something to say, be it a statement or a question. Art is creative, its' inherent nature is to build up. To take that and to make the foundations of it &quot;This thing sucks, I'll show them&quot; is not a point of dialogue I'd want to support.* Do it better? Sure. I'm okay with building on other ideas because we have our own ideas of improvement, I do that rather a lot. But Genius's beginning foundations are spite fueled. I'm not interested in that, no.<br /> <br /> Also, minor note, you'll notice I did not call out any particular game for the entire design by committee. You connected that part of my statement to Genius, not me.<br /> <br /> *I'm not a perfect human being, I succumb to stupid shit all the time, but as a point of comparison, that's why I have an issue with &quot;God I hate the fucking people on these fucking board.&quot;<br /> <br /> EDIT: And, okay, this, let's chat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So? You don't have to respond to and correct everything that people say. That's a bad habit.<br /> I mean, 3 lenghty comments in like half an hour, seriously to like one sentence. -_- Let people think what they do and move on. You guys should go back and delete them. </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry that you feel picked on when, after being a douchebag, people question your behavior.<br /> Maybe you shouldn't blow up other people statements as much as you think other people blow up yours?<br /> <br /> Anyways, petty and juvenille badgering on my part aside, I was quite serious is going back to the main topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-08-2014, 11:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T20:51:20-07:00","id":276037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=276029#post276029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On that note, what happened to the Highlander type (Immortal: Gathering I think?) splat? I heard a rumor that it was removed due to WW's copyright claim (conflicting with Immortals or something?)<br /> I think it may have had a similar set up to what you're asking too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that still up on Mr. Gone's Website? I liked that game, actually-I totally would have played it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T21:11:27-07:00","id":276049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe you shouldn't blow up other people statements as much as you think other people blow up yours? </div> </div> </div>If you are really mature then delete this part now. Otherwise you're just starting to get the last word in some stupid argument that I said from the start I did not want this thread to turn into. Then we can call it quits.<br /> Seriously, how old are you guys? 10?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2330-vree","name":"Vree","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T21:31:24-07:00","id":276057,"title":"","content":"But seriously, did we lose the links to the Highlander Immortal fan-splat? That game was really bulky in a lot of ways and kind of silly on other points, but man did it bring the idea home to WoD despite that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-09-2014, 12:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T21:59:27-07:00","id":276063,"title":"","content":"I'm just the slightest bit curious though.<br /> If Leet was writing Pathogen, what would it be like?<br /> Would it be a Merit-based splat? <br /> A bit more in the halfway area, with a power stat like Purified?<br /> Would it be a purely enemy splat (ie. for quick NPC antagonist creation) or a guide to run a specific type of adventure (infection or zombie but with the traditional WoD splats instead)?<br /> <br /> The guy who wrote it originally created it as an enemy for a campaign, see, and then upgraded it at a player's request who wanted to try to play the things. And even though it turned into an abandoned project even the author himself is still around, so that kind of info would be interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2330-vree","name":"Vree","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T21:59:35-07:00","id":276064,"title":"","content":"As part of the NWoD: Leviathan (with some tweaks of my own)<br /> <br /> As a completely separate setting: Genius","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T22:17:46-07:00","id":276078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=276063#post276063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just the slightest bit curious though.<br /> If Leet was writing Pathogen, what would it be like?<br /> Would it be a Merit-based splat?<br /> A bit more in the halfway area, with a power stat like Purified?<br /> Would it be a purely enemy splat (ie. for quick NPC antagonist creation) or a guide to run a specific type of adventure (infection or zombie but with the traditional WoD splats instead)?<br /> <br /> The guy who wrote it originally created it as an enemy for a campaign, see, and then upgraded it at a player's request who wanted to try to play the things. And even though it turned into an abandoned project even the author himself is still around, so that kind of info would be interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not certain how I would represent it. I think of the Purified as a great template for this sort of thing in their structure. They're some weird powers with some description of the psychology and the little sense of community that they can possess. I think for modeling minor or more unique things (like I think people with some kind of supervirus should be) it's a great way to do it.<br /> <br /> Were I to do it with Pathogen, I'd definitely have to look over whatever the latest draft is, make sure I have a decent idea of the themes of it, then consider what components of it are worth focusing on. Maybe there's a particular write up for one kind of them that's evocative. I'd try to focus on that and turn that one into my mini-splat. I feel like when people make full fansplats, it oftens runs into an issue with say, social groups or contriving the xyz for them where sticking too tightly to that model seems ill advised. It's also just more manageable as a personal project that way.<br /> <br /> This is really heavily influenced by my personal philosophy though, as I always prefer to make a small, good thing than a big thing which might have its reach exceed its grasp, y'know?<br /> <br /> As something more directly related to the question, Leviathan is another one that sounded cool to me in theory, as I have a weakness for spooky aquatic stuff. It's probably my favorite concept for a fansplat straight up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T07:47:59-07:00","id":276341,"title":"","content":"Clearly, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265215-skin-thieves-werewolves-guys-werewolves\">Werewolves</a> are an example.<br /> <br /> I'm working on a kind of Hunter-esque retread of Geist, too, where it's more about solving spooky ghost stories than <i>being</i> the spooky ghost stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T08:26:45-07:00","id":276386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=276049#post276049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are really mature then delete this part now. Otherwise you're just starting to get the last word in some stupid argument that I said from the start I did not want this thread to turn into. Then we can call it quits.<br /> Seriously, how old are you guys? 10?</div> </div> </div> </div>Your original comment made you come off as overly defensive and childish. Honestly that's really the only reaction to get out of someone getting so defensive over what was such an innocuous comment that was so obviously cast as &quot;It's not my cup of tea.&quot; which is far and away from a comment making claims of quality. Personally, I've not a fan splat person either. If I had to choose one to check out maybe Genius or Princess. Princess always seems to have some rpg.net thread and a lot of people talk about Genius here or there, though it's fan base I've seen be over zealous from time to time. Still would be interested some day to see what the buzz is. I'm hoping stuff like Beast provides some more mechanical ideas and tools for fan splat folks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T08:29:20-07:00","id":276392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=276386#post276386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your original comment made you come off as overly defensive and childish. Honestly that's really the only reaction to get out of someone getting so defensive over what was such an innocuous comment that was so obviously cast as &quot;It's not my cup of tea.&quot; which is far and away from a comment making claims of quality. Personally, I've not a fan splat person either. If I had to choose one to check out maybe Genius or Princess. Princess always seems to have some rpg.net thread and a lot of people talk about Genius here or there, though it's fan base I've seen be over zealous from time to time. Still would be interested some day to see what the buzz is. I'm hoping stuff like Beast provides some more mechanical ideas and tools for fan splat folks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tyr, we finally just got back to talking about fan-splats.<br /> <br /> Join us on that conversation.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And then I realize the second part <i>is</i> joining us.<br /> <br /> It's early morning, I'm clearly not working right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-09-2014, 11:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T09:27:00-07:00","id":276421,"title":"","content":"Haven't played it yet but I've been reading Raven's take on Princess and I find myself intrigued. Might use it in the game I'm running.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T09:29:51-07:00","id":276422,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#ff0000\">Lots of personal attacks and thread-capping here, that needs to stop. I'd hate to have to close the thread, so p</span><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">lease </span><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">return to civil discussion of the original topic.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T19:54:00-07:00","id":276928,"title":"","content":"<i>&quot;Fan Splats? My favorite subject!&quot; he typed into the forum as he wistfully stared at his own, woefully incomplete document; the realization of the irony bathing him in miserable self-awareness.</i><br /> <br /> Self-flagellation aside, I find most fan splats to be fairly well-done. Despite some of the fan splats dying out due to lack of interest or drive <i>(I'm still holding out for TvTropes's adoption of <b>Pathogen: the Infected</b>)</i>, the ideas of certain legendary creatures of horror or strangeness is more than welcome for me. Still sad that <b><i>Bogey</i></b> and <b><i>Janus</i></b> haven't been completely fleshed out, though. That said:<br /> <br /> <b><i>Genius: the Transgression:</i></b> My only complaint about this fan splat is that I'm not smart enough to comprehend the construction of Wonders, which is a terrible thing considering that Wonders are the <i>thing</i> that Geniuses do. I do like the themes and overall feel to the splat; the struggle of great intellect tempered by madness is a wonderful topic that I have not seen discussed in many forms of media. The Beholden's are also a great touch <i>(I am not saying that because I imagine Beholdens as Harley Quinn from Batman and Magenta from Rocky Horror Picture Show. It has ABSOLUTELY nothing to do with that at all! How dare you!)<br /> <br /> <b>Leviathan: the Tempest: </b></i>Playable horrorterrors? Where do I sign up? On a more serious note, I find Leviathan to be thematically delicious, meshing the feels of <b><i>Promethean</i></b> and <b><i>Mummy</i></b> together, blending personal horror with godlike presence. However, I wish the presentation was cleaner; as a wiki-based splat, it's incredibly difficult to quickly go through the pages and find the details for Depths or the Vestiges. As a side note, I tend to mix the term <i>Lahamin </i>with <i>Lahmasu</i>, which has caused severe confusion on my part. <br /> <br /> <b><i>Princess: the Hopeful:</i></b> Next to <b><i>Promethean</i></b>, <b><i>Princess</i></b> is one of the few splats that I find to be entirely genuine. Being the beacon in the World of Darkness rather than the candle of the Vigil is a pretty noble aspiration. However, I have made it a personal challenge to vilify the Princesses that follow the Radiant Queens; despite the Twilight Queens being the obvious anti-hero alliances, I wanted to find out if it would be possible to make Princesses antagonists without resorting to political opponents. Granted, <i>Puella Magi Madoka Magica</i> is on my &quot;to-watch&quot; list and Homura and Kyoko seem to be promising leads to build upon in <i><b>Princess</b></i>, but I'd love to find a way to create sinister Princesses without turning them into Dethroned.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Dragon: the Embers:</i></b> The threat of extinction is a double-edged sword. On one hand, it's definitely a fear that humanity itself suffers from and having Dragons react to the <b><i>VERY REAL </i></b>future of dying out as a race is amazing; living in fear of being murdered for their heart and having to isolate themselves is just the delicious icing on the cake. On the other hand, there is no real way to escape this, so the Dragons' existence is just prolonging the inevitable; there doesn't seem to be an ultimate goal beyond survival and conquering humanity <i>(and as the numerous failed villain's schemes to conquer the world have told me, ruling over humanity never works out well)</i><br /> <br /> <b><i>Wraith: the Arising:</i></b> As far as I can tell, dying sucks. Role-playing the dead, however, does not <i>(for the most part)</i>. Although I am not familiar with the oWoD version of <i><b>Wraith</b></i>, I absolutely <b><i>LOVE </i></b>this fan splat with an undying passion. While I love <b><i>Geist</i></b>, it focused more towards the fact that Sin-Eaters were alive thanks to their new best friend. <b><i>Wraith</i></b> kicks all sorts of rear ends when it comes to fleshing out death and I love it, regardless of the conflicts it has with canon.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Hunchback: the Lurching:</i> </b>Is <i>The Hunchback of Notre Dame</i> an iconic monster? <b><i>Hunchback</i></b> is fairly charming in what it is representing; the Miserable are quite miserable and live for their misery. The focus on being an outcast that desires affection is absolutely wonderful and the fact that a Hunchback's existence is entirely set-up to inflict even more misery is hilariously dark <i>(and not at all a reflection of how I view my own existence. Not at all. How dare you.)</i> However, there are parts of Hunchback that are incomplete, such as the Oublier and the lack of a distinct Morality/Integrity stat, that do set the fan splat back. It's a pity, especially since I barely find any discussion of the splat.<br /> <br /> Honestly, despite my concerns due to quality or completion, I love all fan splats and believe them to be integral to the community. The World of Darkness is something of supernatural wonder and fear; specifying the canon splats as being the only supernatural creatures in the setting is fine, but that eliminates many other monsters that exist in legend and in media. I like having options, especially options that have mechanics attached to them.<br /> <br /> Now, if you'll excuse me, I must weep over my <b><i>Shadow: the Perverse</i></b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T15:59:51-07:00","id":277636,"title":"","content":"On fansplats: most seem to either work better as minor templates or occupy the design space of another splat.<br /> <br /> <i>Princess: the Hopeful</i> is probably the coolest and best designed of the fansplats I've seen; it manages to very explicitly define its themes and neatly separates itself from both Changeling and Mage, the two main splats I feel it is closest to.<br /> <br /> <i>Genius: the Transgression</i> is the one I've been told to &quot;check out&quot; the most, and it is horribly disappointing. To me it occupies a very small corner of Mage's design space, it is magic item making Mage lite, has no themes that make it independent (Hubris is Mage, Disbelief/Quiescence is Mage, Eldritch Abominations is Mage, Atlantis/Lemuria is Mage, seeking Truth is Mage in spades, &amp;c).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=276928#post276928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><i>Princess: the Hopeful:</i></b> Next to <b><i>Promethean</i></b>, <b><i>Princess</i></b> is one of the few splats that I find to be entirely genuine. Being the beacon in the World of Darkness rather than the candle of the Vigil is a pretty noble aspiration. However, I have made it a personal challenge to vilify the Princesses that follow the Radiant Queens; despite the Twilight Queens being the obvious anti-hero alliances, I wanted to find out if it would be possible to make Princesses antagonists without resorting to political opponents. Granted, <i>Puella Magi Madoka Magica</i> is on my &quot;to-watch&quot; list and Homura and Kyoko seem to be promising leads to build upon in <i><b>Princess</b></i>, but I'd love to find a way to create sinister Princesses without turning them into Dethroned.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, you are in for a <i>treat</i>. <i>Madoka Magica</i> is fucking incredible, and the <i>Rebellion</i> movie is simply amazing. Second, check out the <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/DarkMagicalGirl\" target=\"_blank\">Dark Magical Girl</a> page for some badguy magical girl ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T14:15:36-07:00","id":278341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=276928#post276928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the struggle of great intellect tempered by madness is a wonderful topic that I have not seen discussed in many forms of media.</div> </div> </div> </div> Try Soon I'll be Invincible. It's one of my favourite books and would fit perfectly as a Genius story.<br /> <br /> (Oh, and Harley is 100% a Beholden)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=276928#post276928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, I have made it a personal challenge to vilify the Princesses that follow the Radiant Queens</div> </div> </div> </div> Let me know if you ever succeed, and I'll patch the Radiant Queens to remove your vilification. Mwahahahaha <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But seriously. In Princess the Radiant Queens are intented to be the example you try to live up to, invidivual princesses can fall and become villianous but the Radiant Queens do not. So I guess, best of luck to you in your attempts <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Puella Magi Madoka Magica has provided a fair bit of inspiration to Princess - but not nearly as much as some people think. I know that most of the setting was nailed down before I watched it (I can't speak for the other contributors) and all of it was nailed down before Rebellion came out. But do watch Madoka, it's awesome, focus on Koyoko since Horuma would be Tears. That said, I consider Sailor Nothing and Mai-Otome to be closer to the spirit of Princess. Sailor Nothing in particular, is IMO, Princesses direct thematic parent.<br /> <br /> Sailor Nothing is the deconstruction, it shows that asking teenaged girls to fight horrific monsters by themselves is a terrible idea. Princess is the reconstruction, responds by asking &quot;why do they have to do it alone&quot;?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=277636#post277636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Genius: the Transgression</i> is the one I've been told to &quot;check out&quot; the most, and it is horribly disappointing. To me it occupies a very small corner of Mage's design space, it is magic item making Mage lite, has no themes that make it independent (Hubris is Mage, Disbelief/Quiescence is Mage, Eldritch Abominations is Mage, Atlantis/Lemuria is Mage, seeking Truth is Mage in spades, &amp;c).</div> </div> </div> </div>But none of those are Genius' themes. If you want to know what seperates Genius from Mage, it's simple.<br /> <br /> Mage is about having power, and how power corrupts.<br /> <br /> Genius is about having no power in the first place.<br /> <br /> To understand how Mad Scientists with rayguns and loyal robot soldiers have no power you have to understand how Genius defines power: &quot;Control, The ability to control your own life and the lives of others&quot;.<br /> <br /> In a game that plays to Genius' core themes* a Genius' fairly modest goal of building an electric car won't just create an Orphan car that goes on a rampage and must be hunted down with rayguns. It will end up creating political and economic chaos as the world shifts from an oil based economy to an &quot;energon&quot; based economy, a few million Africans will be displaced as people realise they're living on top of valuable energon deposits. And the poor Genius will be standing to the side somewhere shouting &quot;this wasn't what I wanted&quot;, and the United Nations can't do anything other than write a sternly worded letter. In other words, much like the savage Hisil reflects a Werewolf's internal rage and savagery. The world of Genius is out of control, reflecting how a Genius' mind is out of control.<br /> <br /> It happens in real life all the time too. How do you think Karl Marx felt about Stalin? And Tim Berners-Lee is quite vocal about the Web.<br /> <br /> <br /> *lets be fair, there's a LOT of Mage games where the players don't get corrupted by their power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T14:36:45-07:00","id":278349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=278341#post278341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But none of those are Genius' themes. If you want to know what seperates Genius from Mage, it's simple.<br /> <br /> Mage is about having power, and how power corrupts.<br /> <br /> Genius is about having no power in the first place.<br /> <br /> To understand how Mad Scientists with rayguns and loyal robot soldiers have no power you have to understand how Genius defines power: &quot;Control, The ability to control your own life and the lives of others&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what you're saying is that, despite a Genius's significantly greater power than a non-Genius, they're still ultimately not in control of the Universe? Almost as if things go wrong in unintended ways?<br /> <br /> How is that different from Mage? The core theme of Mage is that we live in the Fallen World and that there are other, more powerful things out there. Also: Paradox, literally things going wrong and messing up your control.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In a game that plays to Genius' core themes* a Genius' fairly modest goal of building an electric car won't just create an Orphan car that goes on a rampage and must be hunted down with rayguns. It will end up creating political and economic chaos as the world shifts from an oil based economy to an &quot;energon&quot; based economy, a few million Africans will be displaced as people realise they're living on top of valuable energon deposits. And the poor Genius will be standing to the side somewhere shouting &quot;this wasn't what I wanted&quot;, and the United Nations can't do anything other than write a sternly worded letter. In other words, much like the savage Hisil reflects a Werewolf's internal rage and savagery. The world of Genius is out of control, reflecting how a Genius' mind is out of control. </div> </div> </div>Except, mechanically, this can't happen because any mundane that attempts to replicate a Genius's work goes mad in the process or causes the work to go mad: a Genius's works are always one-offs. You're not going to revolutionize the world with a single car powered by phlebotinum, you need a billion (the approximate number of automobiles in the world today).<br /> <br /> Unless the world is nothing but Geniuses. If the goal was <a href=\"http://www.girlgeniusonline.com\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Girl Genius</i></a>: the Game, then I guess it semi-succeeded (though, again, the themes and mechanics don't really enforce that). But then it's not an nWoD setting, it just uses nWoD mechanics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It happens in real life all the time too. How do you think Karl Marx felt about Stalin? And Tim Berners-Lee is quite vocal about the Web. </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> *lets be fair, there's a LOT of Mage games where the players don't get corrupted by their power. </div> </div> </div>Mage is <i>also</i> a game about solving Mysteries and can primarily focus on that, my complaint for <i>Genius</i> is that not only does it not have themes unique from <i>Mage</i> it's not even as broad as <i>Mage</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> [EDIT] Yes, I realize this is mostly hype backlash. If <i>Genius</i> wasn't paraded around so much I'd probably just ignore it or give it more of a break.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 10-11-2014, 05:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T16:21:02-07:00","id":278438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=278349#post278349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what you're saying is that, despite a Genius's significantly greater power than a non-Genius</div> </div> </div> </div> Significantly less power actually. Remember in Genius power is control (honestly, half the reason I use the word 'power' is to contrast with Mage's use of the word).<br /> <br /> Most non-Geniuses are in control of their own brain, Geniuses are not. That said, normal people in Genius don't have much control either. In Werewolf everyone (everyone=Werewolves, hosts and spirits) is savage. In genius everyone (everyone being Geniuses, Manes and mortals) has no control.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=278349#post278349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is that different from Mage? The core theme of Mage is that we live in the Fallen World and that there are other, more powerful things out there.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually the core theme of Mage is power corrupts. It's stated explicitly right there in the introduction.<br /> <br /> The intro to Genius says it's core theme is transgression - which isn't self explanitory like 'power corrupts' but the description does talk about the themes of 'out of control' as I do. It focuses on the individual where I focus on the big picture, but it's the same concept.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, to answer your question. In Genius, <u>no one</u> has control. In Mage, Exarchs and Mages both have control. Exarchs just have more of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=278349#post278349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also: Paradox, literally things going wrong and messing up your control.</div> </div> </div> </div> Paradox is not a core theme of mage, it is a product of Hubris which in turn is part of 'power corrupts'. This is even clearer in the second edition where you only risk Paradox if &quot;your reach exceeds your grasp&quot;.<br /> <br /> Or to put it another way. In Genius your ideas always go out of control. In Mage your magic only has Paradox if you screw up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=278349#post278349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except, mechanically, this can't happen</div> </div> </div> </div> Sure it can. The resources section talks about earning money through mundane inventions. Geniuses sometimes reverse engineer their own wonders to find which bits are sane science and publish them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=278349#post278349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage is <i>also</i> a game about solving Mysteries and can primarily focus on that</div> </div> </div> </div> Genius can also focus on fighting Nazis in zepplins. Exploring bardos. In fact there's two whole sections on different kinds of games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T17:03:48-07:00","id":278468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=278438#post278438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Significantly less power actually. Remember in Genius power is control (honestly, half the reason I use the word 'power' is to contrast with Mage's use of the word).</div> </div> </div> </div>You keep saying that, it's not relevant or even accurate. Do Mages not have power because they are inexorably drawn to Mysteries?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most non-Geniuses are in control of their own brain, Geniuses are not. That said, normal people in Genius don't have much control either. In Werewolf everyone (everyone=Werewolves, hosts and spirits) is savage. In genius everyone (everyone being Geniuses, Manes and mortals) has no control. </div> </div> </div>If Geniuses do not have free will and at least a modicum of self control then they are not appropriate for use as Player Characters. If they do have agency your point is moot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Actually the core theme of Mage is power corrupts. It's stated explicitly right there in the introduction. </div> </div> </div><i>A </i>core theme. <i>The</i> core theme is the Fallen World, that's why it was chosen as the title for the Chronicle.<br /> <br /> And &quot;power corrupts&quot; means that the more power you have the more likely you are to sin... or, to use a different word, Transgress:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The intro to Genius says it's core theme is transgression - which isn't self explanitory like 'power corrupts' but the description does talk about the themes of 'out of control' as I do. It focuses on the individual where I focus on the big picture, but it's the same concept. </div> </div> </div>And they transgress by using their power to alter reality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyway, to answer your question. In Genius, <u>no one</u> has control. In Mage, Exarchs and Mages both have control. Exarchs just have more of it. </div> </div> </div>Mages don't have control and the Exarchs are constantly working to maintain control, it's precarious. If the Exarch's dominion was absolute there wouldn't be Mages in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Paradox is not a core theme of mage, it is a product of Hubris which in turn is part of 'power corrupts'. This is even clearer in the second edition where you only risk Paradox if &quot;your reach exceeds your grasp&quot;. </div> </div> </div>The mechanical expression of the transgression (sin/hubris) of Mages is not one of the core themes of the game line? Wut.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or to put it another way. In Genius your ideas always go out of control. In Mage your magic only has Paradox if you screw up. </div> </div> </div>The mechanics of Genius do not support this, Havoc (which really is caused by little-p paradox) does not always occur. And Paradox can also occur due to Sleepers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sure it can. The resources section talks about earning money through mundane inventions. Geniuses sometimes reverse engineer their own wonders to find which bits are sane science and publish them. </div> </div> </div>Except mundane inventions cannot run on phlebotinum, an impossible substance, so, no, your example couldn't happen and the idea of publishing a purely mundane piece of science is no different than playing a Mortal that makes a discovery. A Mage could construct something from pure magic and reverse engineer it, too. This does not mean that the Wonder or Spell can be mass marketed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Genius can also focus on fighting Nazis in zepplins. Exploring bardos. In fact there's two whole sections on different kinds of games. </div> </div> </div>And Mage could be a game of a future galactic empire, but that wouldn't be the nWoD setting.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T17:31:29-07:00","id":278477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=278468#post278468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>A </i>core theme. <i>The</i> core theme is the Fallen World, that's why it was chosen as the title for the Chronicle.<br /> <br /> And &amp;quot;power corrupts&amp;quot; means that the more power you have the more likely you are to sin... or, to use a different word, Transgress:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well one the chronicle names are not chosen by theme but rather by storyhook.I wouldn't think their core theme is Fallen World, the Fallen World is an obstacle, not the theme. The theme is quite simple,Addicted to Mystery. Mages can't get enough of the stuff, their obsessive. Mages are like bugs to light, they all circle around it,wanting it, but if they get to close, they will get burned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T03:16:21-07:00","id":278697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=278468#post278468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And &quot;power corrupts&quot; means that the more power you have the more likely you are to sin... or, to use a different word, Transgress:</div> </div> </div> </div> This couldn't be more wrong.<br /> <br /> Lets start with the definition of transgression: &quot;An act that goes against a law, rule, or code of conduct; an offence&quot;. You will note that there is nothing automatically immoral about breaking a &quot;law&quot;, a &quot;rule&quot;, or a &quot;code of conduct&quot;. Breaking the law that says &quot;don't murder&quot; is generally immoral, breaking the law that says &quot;slaves should not run away&quot; is perfectly moral.<br /> <br /> In fact here's an even clearer example. Google &quot;transgression against gender norms&quot;. It's a pretty common phrase, and it refers to someone exhibiting a non-typical gender identity. I would <b><u>not</u></b> call a non-typical gender expression a &quot;sin&quot;.<br /> <br /> Power corrupts, however, is a phrase that's universally associated with immoral behaviour.<br /> <br /> <br /> Geniuses don't transgress by doing immoral things, they transgress by being, well, a genius who sees beyond the limits of society. Where as (in Genius) most people think inside the box created by &quot;laws, rules and codes of conducts&quot; Geniuses see beyond the box and ask questions that challange society itself. &quot;Why do women have to be housewives?&quot;, &quot;what would happen if I created a system of communication that would give everyone the same access to information as a professor or government&quot;, and yes - sometime's it is sinful: &quot;what would happen if I surgically removed people's emotions?&quot;<br /> <br /> And if you look at the historical precedent it's always gone out of control. Marxism. The French Revolution. The first wave feminists saw their movement replaced by second then third wave feminism. Note that I am <b>not</b> saying that &quot;out of control&quot; is bad. A lot of people say that third wave feminism is better than first wave feminism. I'm not going to debate that question, it's off topic, but I will argue that the first wave feminists lost control of the movement they created, and that loss of control exemplifies the themes of Genius.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=278468#post278468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mechanical expression of the transgression (sin/hubris) of Mages is not one of the core themes of the game line? Wut.</div> </div> </div> </div> Paradox is just one of many expressions of Hubris. Hubris is just one of many expressions of power corrupts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=278468#post278468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mechanics of Genius do not support this, Havoc (which really is caused by little-p paradox) does not always occur. And Paradox can also occur due to Sleepers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nor do the mechanics of Mage support your charachter becoming less moral as they become power powerful. I don't see this as a problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=278468#post278468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You keep saying that, it's not relevant or even accurate. Do Mages not have power because they are inexorably drawn to Mysteries?</div> </div> </div> </div> I think you can draw a distinction between being drawn to mysteries and being clinically insane.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=278468#post278468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Geniuses do not have free will and at least a modicum of self control then they are not appropriate for use as Player Characters. If they do have agency your point is moot.</div> </div> </div> </div> To use a metaphor. A child has free will, but if their parents decide to move to another town can't do anything about it.<br /> <br /> A Genius is the same. They have free will, but if their wonder ends up causing a war in Africa because some rare earth just got 100 times more valuable they can't do anything (useful) about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T04:36:30-07:00","id":278741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=278697#post278697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> This couldn't be more wrong.<br /> <br /> Lets start with the definition of transgression: &quot;An act that goes against a law, rule, or code of conduct; an offence&quot;. You will note that there is nothing automatically immoral about breaking a &quot;law&quot;, a &quot;rule&quot;, or a &quot;code of conduct&quot;. Breaking the law that says &quot;don't murder&quot; is generally immoral, breaking the law that says &quot;slaves should not run away&quot; is perfectly moral.<br /> <br /> In fact here's an even clearer example. Google &quot;transgression against gender norms&quot;. It's a pretty common phrase, and it refers to someone exhibiting a non-typical gender identity. I would <b><u>not</u></b> call a non-typical gender expression a &quot;sin&quot;.<br /> <br /> Power corrupts, however, is a phrase that's universally associated with immoral behaviour.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also from the Google definition:<br /> <br /> synonyms:<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?client=firefox-a&amp;hs=ghd&amp;rls=org.mozilla:en-US:official&amp;channel=sb&amp;q=define+offense&amp;sa=X&amp;ei=AGQ6VPD6FNbeoASTpoKIDg&amp;ved=0CCEQ_SowAA\" target=\"_blank\">offense</a>, <a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?client=firefox-a&amp;hs=ghd&amp;rls=org.mozilla:en-US:official&amp;channel=sb&amp;q=define+crime&amp;sa=X&amp;ei=AGQ6VPD6FNbeoASTpoKIDg&amp;ved=0CCIQ_SowAA\" target=\"_blank\">crime</a>, <a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?client=firefox-a&amp;hs=ghd&amp;rls=org.mozilla:en-US:official&amp;channel=sb&amp;q=define+sin&amp;sa=X&amp;ei=AGQ6VPD6FNbeoASTpoKIDg&amp;ved=0CCMQ_SowAA\" target=\"_blank\">sin</a>, <a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?client=firefox-a&amp;hs=ghd&amp;rls=org.mozilla:en-US:official&amp;channel=sb&amp;q=define+wrong&amp;sa=X&amp;ei=AGQ6VPD6FNbeoASTpoKIDg&amp;ved=0CCQQ_SowAA\" target=\"_blank\">wrong</a>, <a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?client=firefox-a&amp;hs=ghd&amp;rls=org.mozilla:en-US:official&amp;channel=sb&amp;q=define+wrongdoing&amp;sa=X&amp;ei=AGQ6VPD6FNbeoASTpoKIDg&amp;ved=0CCUQ_SowAA\" target=\"_blank\">wrongdoing</a>, <a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?client=firefox-a&amp;hs=ghd&amp;rls=org.mozilla:en-US:official&amp;channel=sb&amp;q=define+misdemeanor&amp;sa=X&amp;ei=AGQ6VPD6FNbeoASTpoKIDg&amp;ved=0CCYQ_SowAA\" target=\"_blank\">misdemeanor</a>, <a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?client=firefox-a&amp;hs=ghd&amp;rls=org.mozilla:en-US:official&amp;channel=sb&amp;q=define+impropriety&amp;sa=X&amp;ei=AGQ6VPD6FNbeoASTpoKIDg&amp;ved=0CCcQ_SowAA\" target=\"_blank\">impropriety</a>, <a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?client=firefox-a&amp;hs=ghd&amp;rls=org.mozilla:en-US:official&amp;channel=sb&amp;q=define+infraction&amp;sa=X&amp;ei=AGQ6VPD6FNbeoASTpoKIDg&amp;ved=0CCgQ_SowAA\" target=\"_blank\">infraction</a>, <a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?client=firefox-a&amp;hs=ghd&amp;rls=org.mozilla:en-US:official&amp;channel=sb&amp;q=define+misdeed&amp;sa=X&amp;ei=AGQ6VPD6FNbeoASTpoKIDg&amp;ved=0CCkQ_SowAA\" target=\"_blank\">misdeed</a>, lawbreaking; More <a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?client=firefox-a&amp;hs=ghd&amp;rls=org.mozilla:en-US:official&amp;channel=sb&amp;q=define+error&amp;sa=X&amp;ei=AGQ6VPD6FNbeoASTpoKIDg&amp;ved=0CCsQ_SowAA\" target=\"_blank\">error</a>, <a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?client=firefox-a&amp;hs=ghd&amp;rls=org.mozilla:en-US:official&amp;channel=sb&amp;q=define+lapse&amp;sa=X&amp;ei=AGQ6VPD6FNbeoASTpoKIDg&amp;ved=0CCwQ_SowAA\" target=\"_blank\">lapse</a>, <a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?client=firefox-a&amp;hs=ghd&amp;rls=org.mozilla:en-US:official&amp;channel=sb&amp;q=define+peccadillo&amp;sa=X&amp;ei=AGQ6VPD6FNbeoASTpoKIDg&amp;ved=0CC0Q_SowAA\" target=\"_blank\">peccadillo</a>, <a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?client=firefox-a&amp;hs=ghd&amp;rls=org.mozilla:en-US:official&amp;channel=sb&amp;q=define+fault&amp;sa=X&amp;ei=AGQ6VPD6FNbeoASTpoKIDg&amp;ved=0CC4Q_SowAA\" target=\"_blank\">fault</a>;<br /> <br /> Note how <b>sin</b> is a synonym. I don't consider homosexuality sinful, but some people do. And you better believe that the South used religious justification for Slavery, up to and including considering a slave escaping to be a moral fault.<br /> <br /> Also, morality (that thing used to define sin), is a &quot;code of conduct.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Geniuses don't transgress by doing immoral things, they transgress by being, well, a genius who sees beyond the limits of society. Where as (in Genius) most people think inside the box created by &quot;laws, rules and codes of conducts&quot; Geniuses see beyond the box and ask questions that challange society itself. &quot;Why do women have to be housewives?&quot;, &quot;what would happen if I created a system of communication that would give everyone the same access to information as a professor or government&quot;, and yes - sometime's it is sinful: &quot;what would happen if I surgically removed people's emotions?&quot; </div> </div> </div>Other than surgically removing people's emotions (I'm pretty sure it can be done chemically, though) none of those require reality bending powers to accomplish, they're social constructs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And if you look at the historical precedent it's always gone out of control. Marxism. The French Revolution. The first wave feminists saw their movement replaced by second then third wave feminism. Note that I am <b>not</b> saying that &quot;out of control&quot; is bad. A lot of people say that third wave feminism is better than first wave feminism. I'm not going to debate that question, it's off topic, but I will argue that the first wave feminists lost control of the movement they created, and that loss of control exemplifies the themes of Genius. </div> </div> </div>Except those went &quot;out of control&quot; because they were things <i>normal people</i> could use, understand, replicate, and transmit. It doesn't matter how awesome your impossible car is, if people can't replicate it then it won't be revolutionary.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Paradox is just one of many expressions of Hubris. Hubris is just one of many expressions of power corrupts. </div> </div> </div>It's still a core theme and mechanic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nor do the mechanics of Mage support your charachter becoming less moral as they become power powerful. I don't see this as a problem. </div> </div> </div>Mage always supports the idea of the struggle <i>against</i> hubris. You specifically said that in Genius stuff <i><b>always</b></i> goes out of control.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think you can draw a distinction between being drawn to mysteries and being clinically insane. </div> </div> </div>You see things that others don't, you're drawn to things that no one else believes exist, and you have a strong compulsion to figure it out anyway, often at risk of life and limb.<br /> <br /> What's the difference, again?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To use a metaphor. A child has free will, but if their parents decide to move to another town can't do anything about it. </div> </div> </div>And Mages are stuck in a prison-Universe lorded over by transcendent beings. Again, how is Genius different in terms of agency?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A Genius is the same. They have free will, but if their wonder ends up causing a war in Africa because some rare earth just got 100 times more valuable they can't do anything (useful) about it. </div> </div> </div>Except how would this happen? The Wonder is an impossible thing of impossibility, it cannot be made except by that particular Genius (who may not even be able to replicate their own work). A one-off would not impact the world economy that way.<br /> <br /> I could see a Wonder falling into the hands of a criminal syndicate causing a crime wave in a <i>city</i>, but upsetting the global economy? Not unless the Genius can produce a billion copies of their device that don't immediately explode in people's faces.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 10-12-2014, 07:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T08:03:40-07:00","id":278815,"title":"","content":"Hey, while I enjoy the contest as much as anyone(I'm backing Proin), I think we also know this isn't going to go anywhere, and in the mean time were distracting from the main conversation <i>again</i>(Yes, I know, I caused the last one).<br /> <br /> Maybe we can move back to that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T08:10:03-07:00","id":278817,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=proindrakenzol;n278741]You see things that others don't, you're drawn to things that no one else believes exist, and you have a strong compulsion to figure it out anyway, often at risk of life and limb.<br /> <br /> What's the difference, again?[QUOTE]<br /> <br /> In Mage, the things you see and are drawn to are true and important, and your obsession with figuring them out can be fruitful. In Genius - and this is explicit in the text - the things you see and are drawn to are a pack of nonsense, and your obsession with them makes you into a dangerous maniac who destroys the conscience of anyone foolish enough to listen to you.<br /> <br /> Really, that's the only difference between the games. Genius is Mage inverted, Mage where the Banishers are basically right about magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T11:47:20-07:00","id":278961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=278741#post278741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note how <b>sin</b> is a synonym. I don't consider homosexuality sinful, but some people do. And you better believe that the South used religious justification for Slavery, up to and including considering a slave escaping to be a moral fault.</div> </div> </div> </div> Um, what's your point here?<br /> <br /> I said that &quot;transgression&quot; does not require immorality, you said that some people consider homosexuality and escaping slaves to be sinful and that 'sin' is a synoymn of transgression... isn't that what I just said? I even brought up homosexuality and escaping slaves as examples of morally ok transgressions.<br /> <br /> So, what were you trying to say?<br /> <br /> <br /> (For the record, an abolitionist ranting about how Jim Crow wasn't what he had in mind when he fought against slavery would make an awesome Genius charachter)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=278741#post278741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other than surgically removing people's emotions (I'm pretty sure it can be done chemically, though) none of those require reality bending powers to accomplish, they're social constructs.</div> </div> </div> </div> So? Mage is about &quot;power corrupts&quot; or &quot;investigating mysteries&quot;. Neither of those require reality bending to accomplish.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=278741#post278741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except those went &quot;out of control&quot; because they were things <i>normal people</i> could use</div> </div> </div> </div> Again, so what? Like most WoD games Genius uses supernatural metaphors for real issues.<br /> <br /> You could replace wars in Africa with your robot going on a rampage and hit the same themes if you like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=278741#post278741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage always supports the idea of the struggle <i>against</i> hubris. You specifically said that in Genius stuff <i><b>always</b></i> goes out of control.</div> </div> </div> </div> And there is no mechanical issue in mage to force you to face that struggle. If you want to play a saint like hero there's never any moment where you have to &quot;roll to resist hubris&quot;.<br /> <br /> The closest you'd get in mage is the temptation to risk Vulgar spells, on in Mage 2.0, to use too much Reach. If you decided OOC to avoid both, nothing mechanical is going to tempt your charachter into hubris.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=278741#post278741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You see things that others don't, you're drawn to things that no one else believes exist, and you have a strong compulsion to figure it out anyway, often at risk of life and limb.</div> </div> </div> </div> You've just described: Werewolf, Mage, Hunter, Geist and Genius. Arguably Demon and Leviathan too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=278741#post278741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Mages are stuck in a prison-Universe lorded over by transcendent beings. Again, how is Genius different in terms of agency?</div> </div> </div> </div> In terms of agency a genius is a metaphorical child. A Mage is a metaphorical adult. The Exarchs (who's existance will be more questionable in 2.0) are the USA government.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=278741#post278741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except how would this happen?</div> </div> </div> </div> I already answered this one. Geniuses can reverse engineer Wonders to create mundane science. They can also import blueprints from the future. Sell smart-pills to regular inventors. They can provide Wonders to assist in the construction of regular technology (if you're trying to evolve an AI, being able to speed up time helps a LOT).<br /> <br /> Heck, here's a REALLY easy one. Helium 3 mining. Helium 3 has the potentual to revolutionise energy production, the problem is that it's all on the moon. Using Skafoi and Wonders solves that problem, but who knows what mankind will do with Helium 3.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=278815#post278815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, while I enjoy the contest as much as anyone(I'm backing Proin), I think we also know this isn't going to go anywhere, and in the mean time were distracting from the main conversation <i>again</i>(Yes, I know, I caused the last one).<br /> <br /> Maybe we can move back to that?</div> </div> </div> </div>It probably won't go anywhere - but perhaps the best thing would be for a mod to split the thread into two?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T14:25:36-07:00","id":279072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=266314#post266314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a little surprised to see anyone but me remembers Mage: the Indebted. It's a great concept, but as the person who tried to write mechanics for it, I was inexperienced and I think it showed. Annoyingly, I <i>still</i> don't have any idea what mechanic could create the jump from hustler to Bernie Madoff that I want to happen when you go Tier 2 -&gt; Tier 3<br /> <br /> Still, it's nice to see it remembered <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I never could make heads or tails of the mechanics, but for what it's worth, I still love the premise and fluff of Indebted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=266148#post266148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">THe closest I get to liking is Princess the Hopeful. Lot of really good ideas in there that just get framed weirdly. It's very usable, and has some great ideas. Sensitivity is genius.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't help but feel Princess would have been stronger if it just had ditched the Radiant Queens. Don't get me wrong, I really like the Radiant Queens as characters and their kingdoms/courts are very colorful and interesting, but on a whole, they felt like they'd be better suited to a different setting. Personally, just having the Twilight Queens would have presented a more interesting conflict: so you're a magical girl and there are honest to god magic queens and even a whole magic kingdom! The catch? In the face of overwhelming opposition, the queens have all fallen into corruption and now you have a choice to make: will you follow them or will you take a stand against both the queens and the darkness that broke them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":218,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/218-two-shadows","user":"Two-Shadows","date":". 10-12-2014, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/218-two-shadows","name":"Two-Shadows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar218_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T15:25:36-07:00","id":279124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Two-Shadows</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=279072#post279072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't help but feel Princess would have been stronger if it just had ditched the Radiant Queens. Don't get me wrong, I really like the Radiant Queens as characters and their kingdoms/courts are very colorful and interesting, but on a whole, they felt like they'd be better suited to a different setting. Personally, just having the Twilight Queens would have presented a more interesting conflict: so you're a magical girl and there are honest to god magic queens and even a whole magic kingdom! The catch? In the face of overwhelming opposition, the queens have all fallen into corruption and now you have a choice to make: will you follow them or will you take a stand against both the queens and the darkness that broke them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Contrariwise - and perhaps this is just because about seventy-five percent of my mahou shoujo consumption so far is PreCure - I feel like the Twilight Queens took the focus away from the Darkness as a worthwhile set of antagonistic forces on its own; it dramatically collapses the potential for game-localized motif-sets and Alhambra steals heat that could go into developing the various ways the Dark does its work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T16:31:48-07:00","id":279157,"title":"","content":"Princess generally chases a huge number of rabbits(no pun intended) that I'm not sure it has the possibility to catch. I'm saying it doesn't, I'm saying I'm not sure. It's one of those things I struggle with Princess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T16:53:51-07:00","id":279167,"title":"","content":"I feel like Princess would be better with a bit more... modularity in general.<br /> <br /> Like making the basic setting just the Princesses and the Dark, with the different Queens being add-ons.<br /> <br /> You can even still have the three &quot;evil&quot; Princess groups - they are just understandable responses to the horrors of essentially being a child soldier. In that case, I'd make their Practical Magics be something that you could &quot;trade&quot; your normal Practical Magic for - and I'd write a few Umbrae that draw <i>uncomfortable</i> parallels with these &quot;fallen&quot; Princesses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T17:11:49-07:00","id":279181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=279124#post279124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Contrariwise - and perhaps this is just because about seventy-five percent of my mahou shoujo consumption so far is PreCure - I feel like the Twilight Queens took the focus away from the Darkness as a worthwhile set of antagonistic forces on its own; it dramatically collapses the potential for game-localized motif-sets and Alhambra steals heat that could go into developing the various ways the Dark does its work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Think ya hit the nail on the head with that one. When I want neat monsters of the week, I look to the Dark. When I want interesting, in depth antagonists, I look to the Twilight Queens/Courts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=279157#post279157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Princess generally chases a huge number of rabbits(no pun intended) that I'm not sure it has the possibility to catch. I'm saying it doesn't, I'm saying I'm not sure. It's one of those things I struggle with Princess.</div> </div> </div> </div>The game does come off as lacking cohesion. It has all this material that, despite being good on its own, doesn't gel in spite of the games best efforts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=279167#post279167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like Princess would be better with a bit more... modularity in general.<br /> <br /> Like making the basic setting just the Princesses and the Dark, with the different Queens being add-ons.<br /> <br /> You can even still have the three &quot;evil&quot; Princess groups - they are just understandable responses to the horrors of essentially being a child soldier. In that case, I'd make their Practical Magics be something that you could &quot;trade&quot; your normal Practical Magic for - and I'd write a few Umbrae that draw <i>uncomfortable</i> parallels with these &quot;fallen&quot; Princesses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a bad way of going about it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/218-two-shadows","name":"Two-Shadows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar218_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T07:05:08-07:00","id":279605,"title":"","content":"Personally I kind of hate the idea of fan splats because I feel like most of them are just <i>bad</i>. Genius completely misses the tone of the World of Darkness, and it's got all the mechanical stability of a drunken <i>Scion 1e</i>.<br /> <br /> That said, maybe it's just because I've talked with Kings' Raven, or maybe it's just because I like the idea of grimdark magical girls (since playing a Nanoha-esque character was my first RPG), but Princess: The Hopeful kind of grew on me. I almost ran a game of it until I realized that it was kind of unfinished. Although apparently I was looking at a far behind rules set.<br /> <br /> Then again, my favourite games are Geist and Changeling and those have a crap load of &quot;wow, you just really missed the mark here&quot; mechanics and Geist has terrible editing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T08:22:24-07:00","id":279652,"title":"","content":"Some fan splats are good for what they are, but lack the insight into game design that years of experience can give. Compared to what we're used to, they usually tend to be really flawed-but many are good for what they are.<br /> <br /> Others are just bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T09:41:07-07:00","id":279775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=279605#post279605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, maybe it's just because I've talked with Kings' Raven, or maybe it's just because I like the idea of grimdark magical girls (since playing a Nanoha-esque character was my first RPG), but Princess: The Hopeful kind of grew on me. I almost ran a game of it until I realized that it was kind of unfinished. Although apparently I was looking at a far behind rules set.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think part of the issue is that, unlike the main game line, fan splats are developed in public. As such, people may form impressions about the game that cease to be true as it is constructed. Many fan splat threads begin as simply a concept, and as mechanics and ideas accrete onto the original seed, it is compressed by heat and pressure (I'm using a geology metaphor, but it's perfectly acceptable in a social context as well) and thereby transformed into a completely different entity. For instance, the original concept for <b>Dragon the Embers</b> by Shock and Gepetto is only a distant speck now (Y-Splats, 'Ritual' powers, and most of the interpretation of the thematic goals have all changed), and many of the ideas from the first phase of the development were twisted in the second phase and then discarded altogether in the third (and current) phase of development. People who came into the game during different stages of its development will form varying (and perhaps skewed) opinions about the fan splat.<br /> <br /> This open development is a double-edged sword in that manner. If you join in during development, you may be able to influence and tailor the game to your preferences. You will, however, be subjected to repeatedly changing rules and thematic elements, possibly souring you on the whole idea. It's certainly a gamble, and not one with good odds. Still, those always have the best payout, don't they?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T09:44:45-07:00","id":279779,"title":"","content":"I don't think it's a problem of open development so much as crowdsourced development. When we get open dev posts from OPP for instance, the design vision is very clear-cut, and we're arguing over the details and the mechanical components.<br /> <br /> If any of the fansplats demonstrated that kind of clarity of vision and presented it all in one place, that'd be a big help for selling them to folks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T10:12:59-07:00","id":279820,"title":"","content":"The lack of an appointed lead developer is one of the biggest hurdles fan games have to overcome. The presence of one individual with final say over vision and direction does a world of good for keeping the game consistent. Princess is a good example of a game that's been negatively impacted by the absence of a lead developer.<br /> <br /> It also helps to have tested writers, a full development and editing process, dozens of hours of devoted work, and a team small enough not to get muddled with excess input.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T10:21:31-07:00","id":279831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=279124#post279124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Contrariwise - and perhaps this is just because about seventy-five percent of my mahou shoujo consumption so far is PreCure - I feel like the Twilight Queens took the focus away from the Darkness as a worthwhile set of antagonistic forces on its own; it dramatically collapses the potential for game-localized motif-sets and Alhambra steals heat that could go into developing the various ways the Dark does its work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I fully agree with this statement, however as far as I'm concerned it's intentional. It's a deliberate thematic specialisation.<br /> <br /> The Outer Darkness is there to be a simple and straight forward antagonist that serves as monsters of the week or the occasional evil empire such as the one in Sailor Nothing. The Twilight Courts (and Radiant who've got a few dots in Twilight Invocations - that's very common) provide the more complex antagonists.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Two-Shadows</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=279181#post279181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think ya hit the nail on the head with that one. When I want neat monsters of the week, I look to the Dark. When I want interesting, in depth antagonists, I look to the Twilight Queens/Courts.</div> </div> </div> </div> See <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> ------------------------<br /> <br /> One of the reasons I like it this way comes down to the Child Soldiers metaphor that is one of Princess' thematic strands. The problem with child soldiers is not &quot;the enemy might shoot them&quot;. If they had better guns, better training, better strategies, and won without casualties. It still would not be ok to deploy child soldiers.<br /> <br /> When you're focusing on the child soldier metaphor for Princess; then the Twilight Courts represent: The desire to protect yourself and those closet to you (Tears), hatred of the enemy (Storms), and the desire to just escape the horrors (Mirrors).<br /> <br /> These are not bad things (ok, <b>maybe</b> hatred is). They're natural psychological responses. You can't punch them, and you shouldn't punch people just for feeling them. The only correct response is to find a \u201cbetter way\u201d.<br /> <br /> And that's vital. If you're using child soldiers as an enemy the primary antagonist <u>can't</u> be defeated defeated with violence; because the solution to child soldiers is never making the children more effective at violence. It's <u>not using child soldiers</u> (I'm resisting the temptation to add a swear word here)<br /> <br /> In short: An antagonist group that's fundamentally evil just cannot work for the child solider metaphor because violence becomes an appropriate solution. (It can't work for the social activist metaphor either).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 10-13-2014, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T10:52:44-07:00","id":279891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=279831#post279831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One of the reasons I like it this way comes down to the Child Soldiers metaphor that is one of Princess' thematic strands. The problem with child soldiers is not &quot;the enemy might shoot them&quot;. If they had better guns, better training, better strategies, and won without casualties. It still would not be ok to deploy child soldiers.<br /> <br /> When you're focusing on the child soldier metaphor for Princess; then the Twilight Courts represent: The desire to protect yourself and those closet to you (Tears), hatred of the enemy (Storms), and the desire to just escape the horrors (Mirrors).<br /> <br /> These are not bad things (ok, <b>maybe</b> hatred is). They're natural psychological responses. You can't punch them, and you shouldn't punch people just for feeling them. The only correct response is to find a \u201cbetter way\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>...huh...<br /> <br /> When you explain the Twilight Court in a way such as that, I mentally envisioned the Radiant Queens as being a metaphor for the cynic's view on the &quot;benefits&quot; of war. Considering that the Twilight Courts' represent the outcome of being young soldiers, I translated the Radiant Queens as being a representation of the doe-eyed &quot;promises&quot; of war <i>(taking the Clubs ideology: fighting for the betterment of the world)</i><br /> <br /> Of course, I could be reaching for straws here, but that's the image I get.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T12:07:20-07:00","id":279981,"title":"","content":"Straws I'm afraid.<br /> <br /> The Radiant Queens represent that &quot;better way&quot;. Clubs - if we learned to understand each other. Diamonds - if we thought rationally we'd find a mutually acceptable compromise. They're a &quot;better way&quot; that <b>failed</b> to prevent the war. But they worth giving a second chance, and they're a reminder that you can try to find a better way.<br /> <br /> <br /> That said - if you want to twist them into the cynics view be my guest. I'm sure there's some good stories in there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 10-14-2014, 06:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T17:24:59-07:00","id":280279,"title":"","content":"Not Sure if i Replyed... I Like Princess and Genius.. Although I STILL haven't Figured out/Found the Actual Rules for Making the Wonders...<br /> That Said i'm Sorta Working on a &quot;Fan-Splat&quot; Myself... Although i Figured that a Full Splat wouldn't Work so It's likly too end up a Hack for Immortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T20:31:03-07:00","id":281880,"title":"","content":"Yay, Immortal got mentioned. Its in my tag by the way. Hey, Arc, you said it was heavy in parts, would you be willing to give me a heads up on what could use fixing? I've been working on a second edition for some time now and any chance to streamline is always a plus. I can even send you a copy of the new rules (sans splats, been stuck on those for months) if your interested.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T12:04:18-07:00","id":286095,"title":"","content":"A random thought occurs: if you all were going to write Dark Eras for the fan splats, which time periods would you choose for which splat?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T15:30:52-07:00","id":286209,"title":"","content":"Genius: 1960s America, a time of big ideas, big change, and none of them are going to go how their creators imagined. First wave feminism is about to be overturned by second wave feminism. The space race has just begun, nerds study atomic physics and dream of moon colonies, robot butlers, jet-packs and utopias, none will ever be. Meanwhile, unheralded by science fiction, work has begun on ARPANET. The civil rights movement fights the government, but it's real enemy is the looming spectre of drugs. The hippy movement burns bright, but will soon sell out. Meanwhile as the cold war looms, the world itself seems at risk of nuclear annihilation despite everything politicians and diplomats can do to keep it stable.<br /> <br /> Basically - a time of big ideas and enormous change; political, social, and technological. Pick your favourite idea, fight for it, watch it fail like it did in history, see what your charachter learns or doesn't learn from the experience.<br /> <br /> <br /> Princess: England, immediately after WWII. It's a time of shaken national identity as the empire falls apart, a time filled with terrible scars that will slowly start to heal, and it's a time of social activism and sweeping change as people build &quot;a home fit for heroes&quot; and resolve that certain atrocities shall be seen &quot;never again&quot;.<br /> <br /> For similar reasons, the formation of Israel would make a great Princess era - you have people determined to rise above a terrible tragedy and build a new nation for their people. Things like the kibbutz movement trying to find a better way of life, and endless debate about what the new country should be, a new country learning how to handle power and making serious mistakes. But if you're going to have a Princess game set in this era you have to have a chance of creating a lasting peace by around 2000.<br /> <br /> <br /> Leviathan: The Antediluvian era. Half way between Conan the Barbarian and The Bible. The world is Tiamat Herself. We exist in a bubble in an infinite ocean and the ocean is Nu. The only land is on Bahamut's back. It's a bloody bronze age world where the only loyalty is family and the gods reward blind fanaticism and blood sacrifice. But there is hope too, deep on the sea bed (Lahamin) the sky sorcerer Marduk and his disciples teach the values of civilisation. People come from all tribes to learn a better way of life, and to build an enormous tower that will reach above the sea and provide mankind with dry land independent of Bahamut.<br /> <br /> Alternatively: The pacific theatre of WWII. A time of brutal war, chaos, spinning moral compasses, and lots and lots of water. Apocalypse Now would be a good inspiration come to think of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T19:01:23-07:00","id":286296,"title":"","content":"Immortal: the Watchers Chronicle - Paris, 1789, The Reign of Terror - Paranoia, mass social change, riots, and oh yeah Mass Beheadings! its got everything required for the start of a hell of a Gathering. Though to be fair, the whole game is kind of like a Dark Eras chronicle in miniature, I'm thinking about putting in a Interesting Times chapter instead of an interesting places chapter in 2nd Edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T19:32:22-07:00","id":286301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daydreamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=286095#post286095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A random thought occurs: if you all were going to write Dark Eras for the fan splats, which time periods would you choose for which splat?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dragon The Embers: the WWII era in Asia seems adapt. You have Mao and Chiang kai shek fighting each other in the countryside while Japan looms over everyone. It can easily be played as a more modern Romance of the Three Kingdoms with Dragons squabbling, and back stabbing each other in an effort to maintain and expand their rule.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T12:36:20-07:00","id":287914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=266019#post266019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pathogen: the Infected. Never really got past the alpha stage, but damn, that game had a fun texture to it. I love the body horror feel of playing what are essentially fomori with a biological (rather than spiritual) origin.<br /> <br /> Skin sloughing off? Vomiting caustic toxins? Time to suck down energy drinks and the neighbor's bone marrow for just a little more of that sweet, sweet ATP!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually currently working on something like this...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T14:15:33-07:00","id":287975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=287914#post287914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm actually currently working on something like this...</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome,I would like to see what you got.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T21:19:47-07:00","id":290283,"title":"","content":"Janus the Persona since I took a class in psychology also bonus points for using the roman god of doors as a name. Though I do wish that they add more content besides 15 or less pages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":893,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","user":"reaperfrost8","date":". 10-23-2014, 12:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-14T02:27:31-08:00","id":1360850,"title":"","content":"Could someone -PLEASE- just provide links, or at least directions to the following fan-splats?!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Linus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=266099#post266099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Ancients Awaken - The Old Ones Chronicles.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=267079#post267079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;<b>Griffon: the Suffering</b>.&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=267611#post267611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Blood: The Bloodening</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod?p=286296#post286296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Immortal: the Watchers Chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Purified.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-14T11:01:09-08:00","id":1360904,"title":"","content":"<b>Princess: the Hopeful</b> was my entrance from years upon years of reading about the world of darkness, both classic and what would be called chronicles later, into actually playing in the setting. I didn't get far, but I still started. So it has a special meaning to me. I love the idea that the PCs can push back the dark a bit, not that they necessarily will, but that they're able to have a meaningful victory.<br /> <br /> <b>Siren: the Drowning</b> gets the runner up spot from me, and I wish there was a 2e version of it. It isn't perfect, but it has a number of good ideas I would like to see in actual play someday.<br /> <br /> More recently (by which I mean literally today), I've picked up a copy of Beast, to see how well it handles my personal ideas that I want to include, but don't fit as well into any other splat's themes. Lest I have to take to the keyboard and write such weak work as <b>Insect: The Giant</b>* to support my weird fixations on certain themes and archtypes.<br /> <br /> *That was a joke, please don't take that seriously, or interpret anything I've posted as hostile or condescending.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":2598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","user":"Gryphon's Feather","date":". 01-14-2020, 02:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-14T11:13:26-08:00","id":1360907,"title":"","content":"Please read the Beast Players Guide ASAP after tackling the core book. I kinda wish Onyx Path would only sell them as a bundle these days... because the BPG is just that big of an improvement on 